WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.027 --> 00:00:01.350
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.600
- [Narrator] A copy of "War and Peace,"

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.270
a pack of ham with the
word peace written on it

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.420
and a sheet of paper with asterisks.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.480
- I was arrested just for 30 seconds.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.240
- [Narrator] Holding
items like these in public

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.590
could get you in trouble
with authorities in Russia

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.620
under new legislation
introduced in recent weeks.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.640
- What we're seeing now is a near wipe out

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.966
of any ability to speak out.

00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:24.060
(lively music)

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.410
- [Narrator] Moscow puts much effort

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.270
into presenting a well-curated image

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.246
of the war to the population.

00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:32.330
(solider speaking in foreign language)

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.670
- [Narrator] The message inside Russia

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.080
is that its soldiers are defending

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.270
the Ukrainian population

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.143
from their own army and government.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.700
Attempts to question it have been stifled.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.930
The Wall Street Journal
reviewed police documents

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.620
and spoke with people inside Russia

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.670
to understand how far the Kremlin is going

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.230
to control the public's perception

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:51.433
of the war in Ukraine.

00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:54.920
(people chanting in foreign language)

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.470
- [Narrator] In the early
days of the invasion,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.310
people took to the streets across Russia

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:00.430
to protest but within weeks,

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.370
most of the visible signs
of dissent had disappeared.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.070
To understand why, first, we have to look

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.640
at the language the Kremlin is using

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.464
to shape public opinion.

00:01:08.464 --> 00:01:10.080
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.620
When officials in the media
talk about Russia's actions

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.464
in Ukraine, they don't use
words such as war and invasion.

00:01:16.464 --> 00:01:19.114
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:01:19.114 --> 00:01:24.114
(men speaking in foreign language)

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.580
The flip side is people
can be legally liable

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.220
for talking about peace in public

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.491
or promoting antiwar slogans.

00:01:30.491 --> 00:01:31.860
(sirens ringing)

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.640
Like this detention in the
center of Moscow in mid-March.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.300
A young man stood with a sheet of paper,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.500
which at first glance,

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.520
didn't even look like an anti-war poster.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.630
It just showed eight asterisks.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.262
- These eight stars mean

00:01:45.262 --> 00:01:46.095
(Dmitry chanting in foreign language)

00:01:46.095 --> 00:01:48.610
or in English, no to the war.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.690
- [Narrator] Dmitry Reznikov,

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:51.880
a sociology student at
a Moscow university,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.900
is the man seen in this video.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.500
A copy of the police
report reviewed by WSJ

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.780
said that Dmitry
discredited Russian forces

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.803
with his poster.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.070
This is a violation under an amendment

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.520
to existing law that was
swiftly passed in March,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.880
weeks after Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.220
Punishments now include
fines of up to the equivalent

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.640
of $12,000 for discrediting the army

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.300
and up to 15 years in prison

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.800
for publishing anything
deemed to be false information

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:17.743
about the war.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.010
Dmitry was fined equivalent

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.930
to some $600 but he says
his poster has nothing

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.250
to do with discrediting the army.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.960
- My poster expresses two main ideas.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.450
The first one is pacifist position.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.910
The second idea concerns
censorship in our country.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:40.230
Today in Russia, any
publicly expressed opinion

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.420
that contradicts the position

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.490
of the government is a big risk.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.780
- [Narrator] The word peace itself

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.120
is among those that can
discredit Russian forces

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.340
according to prosecutors in the country.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.270
Maxim Selig was fined
the equivalent of $600

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.810
for holding a pack of ham.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.763
He changed the logo to
read peace in Russian.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.830
And Constantine Goldman stood silently

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.090
with a book of "War and
Peace" next to a monument

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.480
to the city of Kyiv near the Kremlin law.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.950
He was detained minutes later

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.550
after a woman reported
him to a police officer,

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.420
found guilty of protesting
near the presidential residence

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.870
and fined according to his lawyer.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.010
All three men pleaded not guilty.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.500
- What this indicates is essentially

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.090
that nothing that might even be taken

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.330
as a sign of dissent is
allowed in Russia right now.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.220
And so if you're even standing

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.770
in a public square
holding a piece of paper,

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.290
whatever that piece of paper says,

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.000
you're signaling to the public

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.657
that you're out there protesting.

00:03:34.657 --> 00:03:38.890
(people chanting in foreign language)

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:41.300
- [Narrator] More than
15,000 antiwar protestors

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.840
have been detained since the start

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.920
of the invasion, according to OVD-Info,

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.580
an independence rights groups.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.680
- It shows the great lengths

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.790
that the Kremlin is going
to to snuff out dissent

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.230
to make sure that its message
of unity behind the war

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.750
is coming across.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.960
- [Narrator] The Kremlin didn't respond

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.330
to The Journal's request for comment

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.220
on arrests of antiwar protestors

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.120
and restrictions on freedom
of speech in the country.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.080
Russian authorities have
said they hear those

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.360
who don't support their actions

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.011
and are working to explain
their goals in Ukraine.

00:04:08.011 --> 00:04:11.940
In April, 74% of respondents
backed Russia's campaign

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:12.930
in Ukraine, according

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.403
to the independent pollster Levada Center.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.340
Some sociologists say opinion polls

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:19.670
aren't necessarily accurate

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.560
in contexts where people are often afraid

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.660
to criticize the government.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.150
Still, in parts of the country,

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:27.020
there continue to be small protests

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.350
and signs of dissent,

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.480
like this no to war sign
that briefly appeared

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:31.970
on the ice of St. Petersburg

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:35.150
and protestors say many
others like them disagree

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.650
with the government.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.370
- The world should know that
there are a lot of people

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.044
in Russia who are against this war.

00:04:42.044 --> 00:04:44.637
(dramatic music)

